    "body": "Two things left over from the spike, both in the same shape of change.\n\n## The scripts were not followed through\n\n`ac85281` removed `fetchNodeProps`, changed `replayIntoScratch` to take one argument and deleted `MintedEdge`. Two callers outside `fragments/` were not updated and do not compile:\n\n- `scripts/read-db-trace.ts` — imports `fetchNodeProps`, calls `replayIntoScratch(history, nodeProps)`\n- `scripts/read-rust-traces.ts` — imports `MintedEdge`, builds a `TraceStep` with `created`/`edges`/`detail`\n\nFour `tsc` errors, the only ones left in the tree. Nothing runs either script, which is why the suite is green with them broken — the same shape as `examples/full-lifecycle.ts` sitting dead for 221 commits.\n\n## \"Which handles did this act create\" is written fifteen times\n\nReading a node id or an edge out of `changes` is now inlined in **eight** places for `NodeCreated` and **seven** for `EdgeCreated`, across `src/mcp/tools.ts`, `src/cli/commands/writes.ts`, `src/cli/views/events.ts`, `src/domain/events.ts`, `src/domain/read/index.ts`, `fragments/replay.ts`, `fragments/trace.ts` and four test files.\n\nThis is the `SUPPORTS`/`CHALLENGES` shape with a bigger sample: that traversal reached six copies, four of them written by the author of the previous fix, and the remedy was to name it once. Two exported functions beside `GraphChange` — `createdIn(event)` and `edgesIn(event)` — collapse all fifteen.\n\nPart of #265.\n",
